        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "You're probably thinking of:\n\n**\"Sit, Ubu, sit. Good dog. Woof!\"**\n\nIt wasn't actually from a specific TV show. It was the closing logo for **Ubu Productions**, the production company founded by \ue200entity\ue202[\"people\",\"Gary David Goldberg\",\"television producer\"]\ue201.\n\nThe logo appeared at the end of several popular sitcoms, including:\n\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Family Ties\",\"1982 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Spin City\",\"1996 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Brooklyn Bridge\",\"1991 sitcom\"]\ue201\n\nThe dog in the logo, Ubu, was Gary David Goldberg's real dog, and the phrase became one of the most recognizable TV production tags of the 1980s and 1990s. \ud83d\udc15 \"Woof!\" \ud83d\ude0a"
          ]
        },
