        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "The **\"Sit, Ubu, sit. Good dog. Woof!\"** tag appeared after quite a few shows produced by Ubu Productions. The ones most people remember it from are:\n\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Family Ties\",\"1982 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Spin City\",\"1996 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Brooklyn Bridge\",\"1991 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Day by Day\",\"1988 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"The Famous Teddy Z\",\"1989 sitcom\"]\ue201\n- \ue200entity\ue202[\"tv_show\",\"Dad\",\"1989 sitcom\"]\ue201\n\nFor many people who grew up in the 1980s and 1990s, the strongest association is **Family Ties**. If you heard \"Sit, Ubu, sit\" as a kid and immediately got a wave of nostalgia, there's a good chance it was after episodes of **Family Ties** starring \ue200entity\ue202[\"known_celebrity\",\"Michael J. Fox\",\"actor\"]\ue201.\n\nDo you remember roughly **what years** you were watching it? That would help narrow down which show you're most likely remembering."
          ]
        },
